==Strategy==
This stage features all nine Mass Production EVAs, who together form a really annoying congregation of enemies alongside the best peon of all time, Metal Doge, who if you don't land a Crit on quickly will cause you to lose. Of course, you don't really need to fight all nine of them, as the last ones spawn almost three and a half minutes into the stage. Conveniently, Bahamut alongside his Explosion is able to land a damage knockback on an EVA in only two hits at level 50, although if your Bahamut is level 40 you'll need a small Attack combo.

At the start of the stage, lure the enemies to your base. After killing the Celeboodle, send out [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Driller Cat]] while the Croconator is still alive. After your meatshields kill the Croconator, your Driller should still be alive. Once Driller lands a hit, which should have insanely high uptime if you also use [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] for a small Weaken combo, send out your Bahamut and watch him dunk on the first EVA, while also spamming meatshields to make sure the swing of the EVAs hits them instead of your Bahamut. Of course, it won't kill thanks to the Metal Doge, so try to immediately deal with it using Critters like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] or [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]. Even if they don't land a Crit in time, Bahamut's outer Explosions should chip onto the first and second Mass Production EVAs, and they should die right there or die after a bit more help from your units like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]. After killing the first EVA, both Driller and Bahamut should be alive, and alongside more meatshields and Explosions the second one should go down fast enough. Around the time the third and fourth EVAs appear, your Bahamut will die, meaning you now need to start using Legend units or Ubers like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] or [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]] to deal with the next EVAs. With this much frontline pushing and Knockbacks from Ururun or Jagando, your units should eventually start hitting the base and destroy the base before EVAs six to nine spawn.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Alongside Talents and a unit for Weakening the EVAs, Bahamut can easily chain the EVAs to death.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]]: For a more endurance-based approach, Jagando can abuse the Metal enemies as stepping stones to spread his Surge onto the EVAs.
*[[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]]: Slower than Cat Researcher, but is easier to obtain.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]: A speedy Critter with rapid attacks who can get decently quick kills on the Metal Doge.
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]]: A fast Weaken vs. Traitless unit who's much easier to obtain and time than Driller.
*[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]]: While his CC isn't as long as Driller or Mightycat, Freeze is a lot better than Weakening the enemies.
*[[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Driller Cat]]: Alongside a Weaken Combo, Driller hits incredible uptime against the EVAs and can easily allow Bahamut to kill multiple EVAs.

===Recommended Ubers===
* [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]]: Using the Metal Doges and Croconators as stepping stones, D'arktanyan can make quick work of EVAs and kill Celeboodle quickly for cash. However, usage of Critters is not recommended if using this unit.
*Generalist Ubers with over 410 range allow you to take a more endurance-based approach towards this stage. Bonus points if they target Traitless as well.

